#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"

Good start! Now turn it into an image that doesn't just look the exact same. I mean turn it into an image with all the same *information* in its 2-dimensional prose and layout and omni-lingual playfulness, then elaborate on that image as if you were a book jacket designer creating the title for a book of the same content we often talk about, and base the cover on all that information in the image, and in the monospaced 2-dimensional unicode content of the text below.

Refer to we.png for layout of the text, and we-cover.png for ideas of what I mean.

Just generate the front cover, straight on, in high detail.

